    intermediate: "The 'Stop' Timing: Don't wait for 51. If you hit 45 or 48 early in the game, call 'Stop' immediately. Your opponents will likely have fragmented hands and won't be able to catch up in a single turn.",
    advanced: 'Market Manipulation: If you have a card that an opponent clearly needs (e.g., they are swapping for Spades and you hold the Spade King), keep it in your hand as long as possible. Only drop it to the table when you can simultaneously pick up a card that completes your own suit.',
    tips: [
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: 'Keep track of which suits other players are taking. If two people are collecting Diamonds, switch to Clubs or Spades to avoid competition.',
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "A 5-for-5 swap is a great way to 'reset' a bad hand if the table has even two cards of a matching suit.",
